        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "185ad7cc-5387-5e30-9371-1e84efbed7bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Columbian Iron Works and Dry Dock Company\n- Places: Baltimore, Maryland; Locust Point peninsula; Fort McHenry; Baltimore Harbor; Chesapeake Bay\n- Events: War of 1812; British attack on Baltimore Harbor\n\nFacts:\n- On September 13–14, 1814, Fort McHenry in Baltimore, Maryland successfully defended Baltimore Harbor from an attack by the British navy from the Chesapeake Bay during the War of 1812.\n- Fort McHenry is a historic American coastal pentagonal bastion fort in Baltimore, Maryland.\n- The Columbian Iron Works and Dry Dock Company operated from 1872 to 1899.\n- The Columbian Iron Works and Dry Dock Company was located in Baltimore, Maryland on the Locust Point peninsula adjacent to Fort McHenry.",
